# Avero AI — Cline Development Rules

## Project Overview
Avero AI is a white-labeled AI assistant platform for small businesses, based on paperclipai/paperclip.
Target market: Small businesses $0–$20M/year.
Brand: Primary #2563eb (blue), Accent #16a34a (green).

## Architecture
- Monorepo (pnpm workspaces)
- packages/plugins/* — agent tool plugins (follow quickbooks pattern)
- packages/db — Drizzle ORM PostgreSQL schemas
- server — Express.js API server
- ui — React + Vite frontend

## CRITICAL: Adapter Type
ALWAYS use `claude_local` adapter. NEVER use `claude-code` or `claude_code`.

## Plugin Development Rules
1. Create plugin under packages/plugins/{name}/
2. Package scope: @paperclipai/plugin-{name}
3. Export AgentTool[] from src/index.ts
4. Use companyId (not userId) for per-company data
5. Register tools in server/src/plugins/index.ts
6. Create DB schema in packages/db/src/schema/{name}.ts
7. Export schema from packages/db/src/schema/index.ts
8. Create migration in packages/db/src/migrations/

## DB Schema Rules
- Always use uuid primary keys with defaultRandom()
- Always include createdAt timestamp with defaultNow()
- Key all company data by companyId uuid
- Follow billing_subscriptions.ts pattern exactly
- Migration numbering: check highest existing number + 1

## Server Routes
- Create route file in server/src/routes/{name}.ts
- Register in server/src/routes/index.ts AND server/src/app.ts
- All routes require authentication (check existing auth middleware pattern)

## UI Rules
- New pages go in ui/src/pages/{Name}Page.tsx
- Register in ui/src/App.tsx
- Add sidebar entry in ui/src/components/Sidebar.tsx
- Use lucide-react for icons
- Brand colors: primary #2563eb, accent #16a34a
- Follow existing page patterns

## TypeScript Rules
- Run `npx tsc --noEmit` before committing
- Fix only errors you introduce — pre-existing errors are known issues
- Strict mode is enabled

## Git Rules
- Branch naming: feature/{name} or bonus/{name}
- Commit format: feat: {description}
- Do NOT push (proxy returns 403) — commit locally only

## Testing
- Unit tests go in packages/{name}/src/__tests__/
- Integration tests in server/src/__tests__/

## Code Style
- Use async/await (not callbacks or raw Promise chains)
- Always handle errors with try/catch
- Log errors with console.error, not console.log
- Use TypeScript strict types — avoid `any`
